e:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min=
-width:fit-content;">A =9351% attack=94 may occur when a group of miners at=
tain more than 50% of the Bitcoin network=92s mining power, thereby enablin=
g them to control the Bitcoin network and protocol and manipulate the block=
chain.  A =93denial-of-service attack=94 occurs when legitimate users are u=
nable to access information systems, devices, or other network resources du=
e to the actions of a malicious actor flooding the network with traffic unt=
il the network is unable to respond or crashes. The Bitcoin network has bee=
n, and can be in the future, subject to denial-of-service attacks, which ca=
n result in temporary delays in block creation and in the transfer of bitco=
in.   See =93Item 1A. Risk Factors =96 Risks Related to Our Bitcoin Strateg=
y and Holdings =96 Bitcoin and other digital assets are novel assets, and a=
re subject to significant legal, commercial, regulatory and technical uncer=
tainty.=94</span></p>
