y:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">For uncertain i=
ncome tax positions, the Company uses a more-likely-than-not recognition th=
reshold based on the technical merits of the income tax position taken.  In=
come tax positions that meet the more-likely-than-not recognition threshold=
 are measured in order to determine the tax benefit recognized in the finan=
cial statements.  The Company recognizes accrued interest related to unreco=
gnized tax benefits as part of income tax expense.  Penalties, if incurred,=
 are recognized as a component of income tax expense.</span></p><p style=3D=
